\frac{\mathrm{P}_{\mathrm{H}_{2}}}{\mathrm{P}_{\mathrm{T}}}=\frac{\mathrm{n}_{\mathrm{H}_{2}}}{\mathrm{n}_{\mathrm{H}_{2}}+\mathrm{n}_{\mathrm{C}_{2} \mathrm{H}}}=\frac{\frac{\mathrm{x}}{2}}{\frac{\mathrm{X}}{2}+\frac{\mathrm{x}}{30}}=\frac{15}{16}
